#
# Consumed in this change (yuvoy-operator#25): managing access from the Team
# screen — `PUT /team/{id}/role`, `POST /team/{id}/hold`, `.../restore` — and
# `DELETE /team/{id}` widening from OWNER-only to OWNER or ADMIN.
#
# ONE BREAKING CHANGE, and it is the reason this bump is not bookkeeping:
# `POST /team/accept` answered `200 {accepted, next}` and now answers
# `201 {joined, next, token, user, operatorId}`. `accepted` is GONE. A client
# reading it gets `undefined`, which is falsy, so a successful accept would
# have read as a failure. Consumed here rather than tolerated: accepting now
# writes the session cookie and lands them inside the portal, the same
# `StartSession` sign-in makes.
#
# `POST /join/{token}/accept` gained the same three session fields, additively.
